      "text_raw": "Copying the expressions of\nthe random offset and the\nCMRR shows that their\nproduct cancels out all the\ndelta terms. Moreover, the\nproduct can be simplified as\nthe input devices are in-\nvolved in an obvious way,\nand also the current source\ntransistor.\nThe resulting parameter is\nmerely the Early Voltage\nV L of the current source.\nE B\nIts value depends on the\nchannel length L chosen. If\nB\nan average value for V L\nE B\nis taken of about 10 V, then some important conclusions can be drawn.",
      "text": "Copying the expressions of the random offset and the CMRR shows that their product cancels out all the delta terms. Moreover, the product can be simplified as the input devices are involved in an obvious way, and also the current source transistor. The resulting parameter is merely the Early Voltage V L of the current source. E B Its value depends on the channel length L chosen. If B an average value for V L E B is taken of about 10 V, then some important conclusions can be drawn."
